@startuml selector-2
' ============================================================================
' Backend selector (2 of 2) — "which libdictenstein backend should I reach for?"
' This figure covers the PREFIX / WORD subtree (you answered NO to the top
' decision, "match substrings, not prefixes"). The SUBSTRING-search subtree —
' the other four backends — is the companion figure selector.puml.
' Color key:  green = always-on in-memory   amber = feature `pathmap-backend`
'             blue  = feature `persistent-artrie` (disk-backed)
'             pale-yellow = the (already-resolved) top decision
' ============================================================================
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam wrapWidth 115
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FFF9C4
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #F9A825
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #37474F

title Choosing a libdictenstein backend — prefix / word lookup (2 of 2)

start
:Store terms\n(optionally\nterm → value);
:Match **substrings**\n(not prefixes)? **→ no**\n(**prefix / word**; substring\nsearch: see companion **selector**);<<#FFF9C4>>

if (Persist +\ncrash-safe?) then (yes)
  if (Native **u64**\nkeys?) then (yes)
    :**Persistent**\n**ARTrie**\n**U64Compact**\n64-bit labels\n(prefix-4 CX);<<#BBDEFB>>
  elseif (Map\n**term ↔ u64**?) then (yes)
    :**Persistent**\n**VocabARTrie**\nbijective\nterm ↔ id;<<#BBDEFB>>
  else (key → value)
    :**Persistent**\n**ARTrie / …Char**\nlock-free\ndurable ART\n(mmap /\nio_uring);<<#BBDEFB>>
  endif
  stop
else (in-memory)
  if (Need\n**remove()**?) then (yes)
    :**DynamicDawg**\n**/ …Char / …U64**\ninsert +\nremove\n(suffix-share);<<#C8E6C9>>
  else (read-mostly)
    :**Double**\n**ArrayTrie**\n**/ …Char**\nfastest,\ncompact\n(BASE/CHECK);<<#C8E6C9>>
  endif
  stop
endif

legend bottom
| Color | Family |
|<#C8E6C9>| in-memory (always on) |
|<#FFF59D>| feature pathmap-backend |
|<#BBDEFB>| feature persistent-artrie (disk) |
|<#FFF9C4>| top decision (resolved) |
endlegend
@enduml
